    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A professional roof inspection in Utah typically costs between $130 and $400, with the statewide average landing right around $190. However, many local roofing contractors will perform a basic visual inspection for free\nif you are planning to use them for subsequent repairs or a full roof replacement.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "between $130 and $400"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost Breakdown by Inspection Type"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The final cost changes significantly depending on the method the inspector uses to look at your roof:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Physical Walk-On ($75 \u2013 $200): The standard approach. An inspector climbs onto the roof to check shingles, flashing, and gutters by hand. Good for straightforward, walkable asphalt roofs.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Drone Inspection ($150 \u2013 $400): A certified pilot uses a 4K camera drone. Best for steep slopes, fragile materials (like tile), or homes with tricky layouts.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6,
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Infrared / Thermal Scan ($400 \u2013 $600+): Advanced thermal imaging detects hidden water pockets and heat loss beneath the surface."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Official Certification ($75 \u2013 $200 extra): An added fee if you need a legal document for a home sale verifying the roof will last another 2 to 5 years."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8,
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Utah-Specific Price Factors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Pitch & Complexity: Utah homes built to shed heavy winter snow often feature steep pitches. Steeper roofs require extra safety gear and tie-offs, adding $25 to $175\nto the baseline labor fee."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Home Stories: A multi-story home adds $25 to $150 to a physical assessment due to extended ladder setups and increased safety risks."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Real Estate vs. Repair: If you need a formal, itemized digital report with photos for a real estate transaction or insurance claim, expect to pay a flat professional fee upfront. If you just noticed a leak after a storm, a local contractor will often check it for free to earn your repair business."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down your options, are you looking for an inspection for a home purchase / insurance claim, or do you suspect active storm damage?"
      }
    ],
